WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:04.780
The MES sends an order to the filling unit of line 3.

2
00:00:05.468 --> 00:00:06.780
You connect that unit.

3
00:00:07.851 --> 00:00:12.286
IT fundamentals teaches you enough to talk with IT about MES,

4
00:00:12.449 --> 00:00:14.260
ERP and the plant network.

5
00:00:15.303 --> 00:00:17.079
Four topics follow the order.

6
00:00:17.797 --> 00:00:21.187
First the road it takes and where the MES runs.

7
00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:26.539
Then where orders and counts are kept and how programs talk to each other.

8
00:00:27.875 --> 00:00:29.675
The first topic is Networks.

9
00:00:30.394 --> 00:00:33.772
Every device has an IP address, like a house number.

10
00:00:34.789 --> 00:00:37.784
The unit hangs on the network cabinet by a cable.

11
00:00:38.531 --> 00:00:40.679
The MES is in another network.

12
00:00:41.745 --> 00:00:45.042
A router carries the order from one network to the other.

13
00:00:46.335 --> 00:00:48.808
The second topic is Servers and cloud.

14
00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:52.716
The MES on the laptop runs on a server.

15
00:00:53.754 --> 00:00:56.668
A server is a computer that provides services.

16
00:00:57.397 --> 00:01:01.043
It stands at the company itself or you rent it in the cloud.

17
00:01:02.121 --> 00:01:06.742
The MES often runs in a virtual machine of its own on that server.

18
00:01:08.052 --> 00:01:10.862
The third topic is Databases and SQL.

19
00:01:11.604 --> 00:01:15.157
The MES keeps orders and counts in a database.

20
00:01:16.296 --> 00:01:18.049
The data sits in tables.

21
00:01:18.763 --> 00:01:22.130
Each row is one order and each column is one property.

22
00:01:23.136 --> 00:01:25.679
With a query you read which orders are in it.

23
00:01:27.017 --> 00:01:29.803
The fourth topic is Software and APIs.

24
00:01:30.538 --> 00:01:34.021
The laptop is the client and asks, the server answers.

25
00:01:35.021 --> 00:01:37.122
The order comes from the ERP.

26
00:01:37.817 --> 00:01:41.544
An API is the agreed way programs talk to each other.

27
00:01:42.555 --> 00:01:46.955
You usually open the MES as a web application in the browser.

28
00:01:47.962 --> 00:01:49.715
So the order finds the unit.

29
00:01:50.627 --> 00:01:52.682
Then you connect it step by step.

30
00:01:54.014 --> 00:01:54.827
The whole map.

31
00:01:55.573 --> 00:01:59.741
IT fundamentals is the first station of Automation and IT.

32
00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:02.470
Every topic has four levels.

33
00:02:03.478 --> 00:02:07.530
Start with IP addresses, LAN and DNS at Basics level.

34
00:02:08.258 --> 00:02:11.277
That lesson shows how messages find their device.

35
00:02:12.289 --> 00:02:16.004
At Working knowledge level come ports, the forms of cloud,

36
00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:18.303
filtering data and interfaces.

37
00:02:19.343 --> 00:02:21.653
At Advanced level come the OT network,

38
00:02:21.851 --> 00:02:25.473
backups, reports that disagree and interfaces that break.

39
00:02:26.529 --> 00:02:30.755
At Expert level it is about judging a network, what an outage costs,

40
00:02:30.929 --> 00:02:32.671
double counting and updates.

41
00:02:33.693 --> 00:02:37.873
Every lesson and every film in this module has a place on this map.
